      "node_id": "kg_doc_5",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Title: The Twenty-fifth Anniversary Anthology. The Twenty-fifth Anniversary Anthology is a compilation album released by The Fixx in 2006 in celebration of their 25th anniversary. It contains singles, album and live tracks from their previous albums, together with a cover version of Nancy Sinatra's \"These Boots Are Made for Walkin'\" that was originally recorded for the multi-artist album \"When Pigs Fly: Songs You Thought You'd Never Hear\". The eight page booklet contains an essay by Josh Norek.",
